---
// Figure: a crash between the commit and the delete, with the application deleting or an outbox relay.
import SimFigure from '../shared/SimFigure.astro';
import Choice from '../shared/Choice.astro';
interface Props { number: number }
const { number } = Astro.props;
---
<SimFigure number={number} id="inv-outbox" title="A crash between the commit and the delete" controls="steps"
  caption="A sequence of steps, not a timed simulation. The relay could poll an outbox table or read the database's change log; either way it works from what the database committed. How long the relay takes is not shown.">
  <Choice slot="params" name="via" label="The delete is sent by" value="app"
    options={[{ value: 'app', label: 'the writer itself' }, { value: 'outbox', label: 'a relay reading an outbox' }]} />
  <Fragment slot="text">
    <p>The writer itself: the writer commits £35 and dies before sending the delete. Readers get £39 from Redis until the copy expires; nothing else knows it is old.</p>
    <p>A relay reading an outbox: in one transaction the writer changes the price and inserts an outbox row saying "invalidate product:42", then dies. The relay picks up the row, deletes product:42 from Redis and marks the row done. If it crashed before marking the row it would delete again after restarting, which is harmless. The next read misses and caches £35. The delete arrives later than the writer's would have, but it arrives once the relay is running, even though the writer died.</p>
  </Fragment>
</SimFigure>
<script>
  import { switchSequence } from './switch-sequence.mjs';
  import { outboxSpecs } from './sequences.mjs';
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-figure-id="inv-outbox"]').forEach(root => switchSequence(root, outboxSpecs, 'via'));
</script>
